@startuml spec-architecture-taskflow
title TaskFlow — Target Component Architecture (Dioxus, desktop local-first)
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "presentation (Dioxus RSX)" {
  [Dashboard]
  [Todos page\n(list/board/table views)]
  [Tasks Kanban + calendar]
  [Subtasks / Categories]
  [Stats page (charts)]
  [Auth pages\n(login/register/change-password)]
  [Chat UI / rooms sidebar]
  [Settings / About / Data-mgmt]
}

package "application" {
  [Todo/Task/Subtask handlers\n+ real current_user.id]
  [CascadeService\ndelete/restore/batch]
  [VisibilitySync\nchange_todo_visibility]
  [PermissionGate\nevery read/write]
  [AuthService\nbcrypt + JWT-shaped session]
  [StatisticsEngine\nwindows, analytics, charts]
  [ActivityRecorder]
  [Search & filters]
  [Notifications]
  [Group/Room/DM service]
  [Chat message service]
}

package "domain" {
  database "Pure rules" {
    [Permission decision table\nVIEWER<EDITOR<MOD<OWNER,\ndefault role "viewer"]
    [Cascade relation graph\ntodos->tasks->subtasks->comments]
    [Kanban order math\norder = len-1-index]
    [Statistics formulas\ncompletion %, avg hours,\nproductivity score, change %]
    [Entities: todo/task/subtask/\ncategory/chat/comment/group/\nroom/profile/user/notification]
  }
}

package "infrastructure" {
  [BaseCrudService over JSON provider\ncollections: todos tasks subtasks categories\nchats comments groups rooms users profiles\nnotifications daily_activities schemas\nunder app_data_dir]
  [Deleted-at archive store\n(soft-delete surface)]
  [Backup/export routines]
}

[Dashboard] --> [StatisticsEngine]
[Tasks Kanban + calendar] --> [Kanban order math\norder = len-1-index]
[Todo/Task/Subtask handlers\n+ real current_user.id] --> [PermissionGate\nevery read/write]
[CascadeService\ndelete/restore/batch] --> [Cascade relation graph\ntodos->tasks->subtasks->comments]
[StatisticsEngine\nwindows, analytics, charts] --> [Statistics formulas\ncompletion %, avg hours,\nproductivity score, change %]
[VisibilitySync\nchange_todo_visibility] --> [Cascade relation graph\ntodos->tasks->subtasks->comments]
[ActivityRecorder] --> [BaseCrudService over JSON provider\ncollections: todos tasks subtasks categories\nchats comments groups rooms users profiles\nnotifications daily_activities schemas\nunder app_data_dir]
[Todo/Task/Subtask handlers\n+ real current_user.id] --> [BaseCrudService over JSON provider\ncollections: todos tasks subtasks categories\nchats comments groups rooms users profiles\nnotifications daily_activities schemas\nunder app_data_dir]
[AuthService\nbcrypt + JWT-shaped session] --> [BaseCrudService over JSON provider\ncollections: todos tasks subtasks categories\nchats comments groups rooms users profiles\nnotifications daily_activities schemas\nunder app_data_dir]

note bottom of [BaseCrudService over JSON provider\ncollections: todos tasks subtasks categories\nchats comments groups rooms users profiles\nnotifications daily_activities schemas\nunder app_data_dir]
  Master's Mongo dual-provider routing
  (private -> JSON, shared/public -> Mongo,
  OFFLINE_MODE override) is intentionally reduced
  to the single JSON provider; collection names
  and document shapes stay at parity.
end note
@enduml
